Lab #15 – Blind SQL Injection with Out-of-Band Interaction

Vulnerable Parameter:

Tracking cookie

Goal:

Trigger a DNS lookup using SQL injection.

Analysis:

The application did not show errors or query results.
I injected an out-of-band SQL payload into the TrackingId cookie.
The payload forced the database server to make a request to my Burp Collaborator domain.
Burp Collaborator received a DNS interaction from the target server.

Result:

Successfully confirmed the blind SQL injection vulnerability.

Key Takeaway:

When no errors or data are visible, out-of-band interactions like DNS lookups can be used to verify SQL injection.

Mitigation:

Use parameterized queries.
Validate user input.
Restrict outbound network access from database servers.
Apply least-privilege permissions.
